{"name":"Kiss of a Vampire","hex":"#8a0009","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch with the lips or press the lips against, usually to show love or affection or passion, or as part of a greeting.","To (cause to) touch lightly or slightly; to come into contact."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A touch with the lips, usually to express love or affection, or as a greeting.","An 'X' mark placed at the end of a letter or other type of message, signifying the bestowal of a kiss from the sender to the receiver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss"},{"term":"vampire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythological creature (usually humanoid and undead) said to feed on the blood or life energy of the living. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person with habits traditionally ascribed to (literal) vampires, such as heliophobia, being a night owl, having pale skin, and so on."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To drain of energy or resources."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vampire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss","wikidata":"Q7307"},{"title":"Vampire","blocks":[{"text":"A vampire is a mythical creature with a human-like appearance that subsists by feeding on the vital essence of humans. In European folklore, vampires are undead humanoid creatures that visit loved ones and cause mischief or deaths in the neighbourhoods they inhabited while they were alive. They wear shrouds and are often described as bloated and of ruddy or dark countenance, contrasting with the modern gaunt, pale vampire which dates from the early 19th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg/330px-Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire","wikidata":"Q46721"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/500px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/1280px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/500px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A forehead kiss","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSMC-16853.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/US_Navy_060105-N-3019M-002_Boatswain%27s_Mate_3rd_Class_Leroy_Quinn_kisses_his_son_on_the_pier_before_departing_aboard_the_guided_missile_destroyer_USS_Chung-Hoon_%28DDG_93%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/US_Navy_060105-N-3019M-002_Boatswain%27s_Mate_3rd_Class_Leroy_Quinn_kisses_his_son_on_the_pier_befo